WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.292 --> 00:00:07.712
I join you from Lagos, Nigeria,

00:00:08.797 --> 00:00:11.132
one of the largest cities in Africa.

00:00:11.967 --> 00:00:15.762
By 2050, Lagos will outgrow
many of the largest cities of the world,

00:00:15.762 --> 00:00:17.722
including New York and Mexico City,

00:00:17.764 --> 00:00:20.559
and will be home
to over 32 million people.

00:00:21.142 --> 00:00:22.644
By that same date,

00:00:22.644 --> 00:00:26.064
Nigeria will be home to more people
than the United States.

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:28.608
But there is a problem.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:33.446
Lagos and other African megacities
suffer, or are plagued by,

00:00:33.446 --> 00:00:36.950
limited road infrastructure, pollution,

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:39.369
congestion and poor safety conditions.

00:00:40.662 --> 00:00:43.582
This makes it very difficult
for people to get to work,

00:00:43.582 --> 00:00:46.334
especially in low-income communities,

00:00:46.376 --> 00:00:50.630
where poverty infrastructure
gaps are pervasive.

00:00:51.881 --> 00:00:54.718
Enter the African motorcycle taxi driver.

00:00:54.759 --> 00:00:56.803
Driving on two and three wheels,

00:00:56.845 --> 00:00:59.598
they race through the congested
streets of Africa,

00:00:59.639 --> 00:01:02.767
getting people and goods
to where they need to be.

00:01:03.518 --> 00:01:07.230
Unfortunately, these drivers
are excluded from the formal economy.

00:01:08.023 --> 00:01:12.193
Unable to afford to buy
clean, efficient vehicles,

00:01:12.235 --> 00:01:16.781
they are left to rent old gas engines
from exploitative loan sharks.

00:01:18.199 --> 00:01:23.496
Because of this tough situation
that these drivers endure,

00:01:23.538 --> 00:01:26.082
they are often left
to fend for themselves.

00:01:27.417 --> 00:01:29.419
Part of what they also endure and suffer

00:01:29.419 --> 00:01:33.673
is high cost of operations
from these exploitative loan sharks.

00:01:34.424 --> 00:01:36.968
And also, these drivers
pollute the environment.

00:01:37.636 --> 00:01:39.471
If nothing is done,

00:01:39.512 --> 00:01:42.349
pollution from two-
and three-wheeled vehicles in Africa

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:45.769
will hit 1.7 gigatonnes
of emissions every year,

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:47.854
according to our estimates.

00:01:47.896 --> 00:01:54.110
This is equivalent to pollution
from two million Boeing 737 airplanes,

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:55.570
every single year.

00:01:56.613 --> 00:02:00.492
I left my engineering job
in 2013 to go to MIT,

00:02:00.492 --> 00:02:03.662
where I met my cofounder, Chinedu Azodoh,

00:02:03.703 --> 00:02:06.206
a fellow engineer with similar dreams.

00:02:06.831 --> 00:02:10.585
We bonded about the realization
that Africa was being left behind

00:02:10.585 --> 00:02:13.505
in the global transition
to clean mobility.

00:02:15.256 --> 00:02:18.259
Inspired by the work
of other innovators around the world,

00:02:18.301 --> 00:02:22.472
we chose to embark on a journey
to create a three-part solution,

00:02:22.472 --> 00:02:28.853
which provides motorcycle taxi drivers
in Africa access to electric vehicles,

00:02:28.895 --> 00:02:31.189
battery swaps and maintenance

00:02:31.189 --> 00:02:33.274
and also emergency assistance.

00:02:34.275 --> 00:02:36.027
Here is how it works.

00:02:36.027 --> 00:02:39.489
Drivers sign up on the platform

00:02:39.531 --> 00:02:43.243
and instantly, they get access
to an electric motorcycle

00:02:43.284 --> 00:02:44.953
and a full battery swap.

00:02:45.954 --> 00:02:48.581
So therefore, they're able to save up

00:02:48.581 --> 00:02:50.667
and earn money to buy those vehicles.

00:02:51.292 --> 00:02:53.962
In addition, we also help
lower their risks

00:02:53.962 --> 00:02:57.215
by providing them access
to emergency response,

00:02:57.257 --> 00:03:00.051
health insurance and maintenance plans.

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:03.221
This represents an integrated approach

00:03:03.221 --> 00:03:06.224
to the design, manufacturing,

00:03:06.266 --> 00:03:09.853
financing and operations
of an electric mobility platform

00:03:09.853 --> 00:03:15.024
targeted at highly vulnerable, informal
and unbanked people groups.

00:03:16.276 --> 00:03:18.236
The revenue from the drivers

00:03:18.236 --> 00:03:21.322
covers the cost of the electric fleet
and the batteries,

00:03:21.364 --> 00:03:25.285
while the cost of R and D and technology
is covered by our partners,

00:03:25.326 --> 00:03:28.329
including foundations,
nonprofits and investors.

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:32.959
Meet Baba Gbenro, one of our drivers.

00:03:33.001 --> 00:03:34.794
Before signing up on our platform,

00:03:34.836 --> 00:03:38.006
he was a smallholder farmer,
earning three dollars a day

00:03:38.047 --> 00:03:41.468
in the Gbamu Gbamu community
in southwestern Nigeria.

00:03:41.468 --> 00:03:45.096
Tragedy struck when 
Baba Gbenro lost his first son.

00:03:45.472 --> 00:03:49.726
Without help, he struggled
to transport farm produce

00:03:49.768 --> 00:03:51.728
and therefore could not make ends meet.

00:03:52.353 --> 00:03:54.439
After signing up on our platform,

00:03:54.439 --> 00:03:57.233
he immediately got access
to an electric motorcycle

00:03:57.233 --> 00:03:59.778
plus a fully charged battery
on a daily basis.

00:04:00.278 --> 00:04:05.283
This enabled him to be able
to transport people in his community,

00:04:05.283 --> 00:04:06.951
make a little bit more money

00:04:06.951 --> 00:04:08.495
and also meet his obligations,

00:04:08.536 --> 00:04:11.039
including sending
his younger son to school.

00:04:11.039 --> 00:04:13.541
Our platform enabled him
to increase his net income,

00:04:13.541 --> 00:04:14.709
on a daily basis,

00:04:14.751 --> 00:04:17.003
from three dollars to six dollars.

00:04:17.962 --> 00:04:23.009
To date, our platform has served
a network of over 15,000 drivers,

00:04:23.051 --> 00:04:26.971
and our data shows that the average driver
has about five dependents,

00:04:26.971 --> 00:04:31.518
meaning that our work has likely impacted
over 75,000 livelihoods.

00:04:32.352 --> 00:04:33.978
By 2025,

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:36.898
our goal is to provide
electric mobility solutions

00:04:36.898 --> 00:04:39.234
to over 150,000 of drivers.

00:04:39.692 --> 00:04:42.403
And if this idea really takes off,

00:04:42.403 --> 00:04:46.199
electric mobility innovators
and climate entrepreneurs in Africa

00:04:46.199 --> 00:04:51.830
could jointly impact over 10 million
motorcycle taxi drivers.

00:04:52.872 --> 00:04:55.083
By doing this,

00:04:55.083 --> 00:04:58.753
we will be helping to move
the world's youngest

00:04:58.753 --> 00:05:00.672
and fastest-growing continent

00:05:00.713 --> 00:05:05.176
towards a more sustainable
and a prosperous future,

00:05:05.218 --> 00:05:08.471
and we will be creating jobs
and reducing emissions.

00:05:08.972 --> 00:05:10.181
Thank you very much.

00:05:10.181 --> 00:05:12.392
(Cheers and applause)

